[
  "Welcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter Philosophy, Empathy & Craftsmanship. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers met face to face to establish standards of craftsmanship. Today we rewatch Episode 21: Greg Baugues from RailsConf 2014 (2014).",
  "Greg was a Chicago developer advocate, organizer, and former 8th Light apprentice whose landmark talk at RailsConf Chicago created the most impactful corridor conversation in conference history.",
  "What inspired Greg Baugues to stand up before thousands of developers and break the silence around ADHD, bipolar, and mental health in software engineering? What principles guided Greg Baugues when this conversation was recorded? How do those lessons inform the software systems we design today?",
  "Roll archive footage (YouTube ID: d8c9ZQ7lAtY). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "Neurodiversity is a core reality of engineering teams. Sustainable pacing, psychological safety, and honest vulnerability remain human responsibilities no model can replace. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
  "Thank you for joining today's session. Full transcripts, provenance notes, and companion research are available at just3ws.com. In our next broadcast, we explore Episode 22. Until next time, keep your feedback loops fast and your code humane."
]